1
00:00:03,261 --> 00:00:07,020
The Executive performance dashboard shows the main numbers.

2
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:09,796
Interactions counts every call or message.

3
00:00:09,796 --> 00:00:14,943
Inbound offered counts the inbound ones, and Inbound answered counts those an agent

4
00:00:14,943 --> 00:00:17,371
took, with the answer rate under it.

5
00:00:17,975 --> 00:00:23,275
Abandoned is a caller who hung up while waiting, or while an agent was ringing.

6
00:00:23,275 --> 00:00:27,079
Its percentage is abandoned divided by inbound offered.

7
00:00:27,079 --> 00:00:33,315
Voicemail and Callback requested are neither answered nor abandoned, so each has its own card.

8
00:00:33,931 --> 00:00:37,487
Failed is a call that failed for a technical reason.

9
00:00:37,487 --> 00:00:42,268
Average speed of answer is how long inbound callers waited for an agent.

10
00:00:42,268 --> 00:00:47,111
Average handle time is the talk, hold and wrap-up time of a handled call.

11
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:51,930
Transfer rate is the share of answered calls that were transferred.

12
00:00:51,930 --> 00:00:56,855
Recording coverage is the share of answered voice calls that have a recording.

13
00:00:56,855 --> 00:01:01,839
Charts below show the daily trend, the channel mix, each queue's service level,

14
00:01:01,839 --> 00:01:03,540
and the busiest agents.

